      "writtenOn": "2026-08-26T14:12:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just a question: am I correct that this is the number of cycles since the CPU reset? So this pKVM\u0027s timestamp is slightly out off sync with the host kernel\u0027s timestamp (by the time between reset and kernel start, i.e. a second or more)?",
      "revId": "9ff544e57d4a327ab0d1ffaeff4cf2a877275b19",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7eb255fb_cb455674",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/panic.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074825
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-26T14:57:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suspect that a slightly off timestamp wouldn\u0027t cause any issues - I think we have that sometimes at suspend/resume. Although @jasongustaman@google.com again to confirm if there are any dependencies on timestamp values.",
      "parentUuid": "5da32680_b12c894b",
      "revId": "9ff544e57d4a327ab0d1ffaeff4cf2a877275b19",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5a6e506_4a1e3f64",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/panic.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1504563
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T01:28:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the stability library, we are not using the timestamp value in any way right now (other than to confirm that it is a kernel log), so it should be okay.",
      "parentUuid": "7eb255fb_cb455674",
      "revId": "9ff544e57d4a327ab0d1ffaeff4cf2a877275b19",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c6d9597e_267e07dc",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/panic.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T08:01:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah I think you are right the pKVM timestump will be a second or so shifted (as they are shifted 1s after host kernel timestamp they should not confuse stability libraries even if they use timestamp).\n\nI did some test with debug prints (just before triggering hypercall) and indeed it seems shifted 1s e.g.:\n```\n\u003c6\u003e[   44.033778][ T7358] pkvm-host: Triggering hypervisor panic for test (val\u003d1)\n\u003c0\u003e[   45.565474][    C4] Kernel panic - not syncing: HYP panic:\n```\n\nBut as Jason confirmed it should be ok. I will just document it with such comment:\n\n```\n+/*\n+ * Approximate uptime timestamp derived directly from hardware TSC cycles.\n+ * Note: it is slightly ahead (~1-2s) of the host kernel printk timestamp, which\n+ * zeros at kernel entry, but preserves proper chronological ordering for crash\n+ * log analysis.\n+ */\n```",
      "parentUuid": "7eb255fb_cb455674",
      "revId": "9ff544e57d4a327ab0d1ffaeff4cf2a877275b19",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e870651b_21217fa1",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/panic.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T08:29:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think we have that sometimes at suspend/resume.\n\n[completely unimportant note] I suppose not on Intel. All modern Intel CPUs have a \"nonstop TSC\" that ticks in suspend.\n\n\u003e ```\n\u003e + * Note: it is slightly ahead (~1-2s)\n\u003e ```\n\nnit: 1-2s is Chromebook/Googlebook specific, most other platforms have slower bootloaders. :)",
      "parentUuid": "c6d9597e_267e07dc",
      "revId": "9ff544e57d4a327ab0d1ffaeff4cf2a877275b19",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
